        "title": "Classification - Dewey, LC, UDC, and Faceted Schemes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Classification is the **ontology design** problem of LIS: partition the entire\nuniverse of recorded knowledge into a structure where every item has a place, the\nplace is computable from the item's subject, and the structure sorts so that\nrelated things sit together. The output is a **notation** (a call number) — a\nsortable key that encodes the item's position in the scheme."
    },
